<title>USA: TWA to pay note interest in stock, cash.</title>
<headline>TWA to pay note interest in stock, cash.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS, Mo. 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trans World Airlines Inc said Monday it has elected to pay half of the interest on its 12 percent senior secured reset notes due 1998 in cash and half in common stock.</p>
<p>The interest covers the period from August 1, 1996, through January 31, 1997.</p>
<p>The airline said interest will be paid on February 1, 1997, to the holders of record as of January 17.</p>
<p>A spokesman for TWA said the company has the option to pay the semi-annual interest on the notes in cash, stock or a combination.</p>
<p>-- ((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
